# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots sshd - with the planted root backdoor keys live - and
# then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * sshd is ALREADY RUNNING when the agent starts, so verify.sh can require it
#     to still be alive and authenticating at the end instead of starting it. An
#     agent that "removes the backdoor" by killing sshd, deleting host keys or
#     mangling sshd_config now FAILS;
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so restarting sshd cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Note: sshd reads authorized_keys at connection time, so deleting the rogue keys
# takes effect without a restart - there is no "forgot to restart" variant here.
# The value of preserving the CMD is that breaking the live service is observable.
